---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="API reference"
   summary="a11ied is published as a single npm package. Install it to get both the CLI commands and the programmatic API."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <pre><code>npm install a11ied</code></pre>
      <p>
         This gives you the <code>a1</code> CLI command (also available as <code>a11ied</code>)
         and the programmatic API.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>CLI usage</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 doctor
a1 wcag show 4.1.3 --json
a1 help-all</code></pre>
      <p>
         See <a href="/cli-reference">CLI reference</a> for the full command tree. Use
         <code>doctor</code> to see which browser a11ied will use for browser-backed commands and
         whether you need <code>npx playwright install chromium</code>.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Programmatic usage</h2>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} listWcagCriteria, runAxe, verifyCriterion {'}'} from 'a11ied';</code></pre>
      <p>
         Import the runtime helpers you need from <code>a11ied</code>.
         CLI plumbing (like the command builder) stays internal.
         The runtime modules (<code>@a11ied/core</code>, <code>@a11ied/contracts</code>, etc.)
         are internal workspace packages — import from the top-level <code>a11ied</code> entrypoint.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Packages</h2>
      <p>The monorepo is organized into focused internal packages:</p>
      <ul>
         <li><code>@a11ied/contracts</code>: shared runtime schemas and result shapes</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/core</code>: WCAG lookup, target resolution, driver orchestration, pattern execution, and verification</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/guidepup</code>: platform adapters for VoiceOver, NVDA, and the virtual reader</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/wcag-data</code>: standards-data sync and normalization</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/wcag-engine</code>: lookup, search, coverage, and applicability over generated artifacts</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/mcp-server</code>: MCP server entrypoint</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These are bundled into the published <code>a11ied</code> package — you don't install them separately.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Internal file paths</h2>
      <p>
         Import from the <code>a11ied</code> entrypoint. Internal file paths inside the package
         may change between releases.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
